# ignore: the global gitignore (~/.config/git/ignore), read by every
# repository.  Editor, OS and coding-agent leftovers only: a project's own
# build output belongs in its .gitignore, so everyone who clones it gets that
# too.
#
# Each setting has its description in the comment above it.  A setting with
# "#" directly in front of it is off: delete that "#" to turn it on, or add
# one to turn a setting off.  `dots options WORD` searches every file.
# A pattern here hides matching files in every repository, including files
# a project meant to commit.

# Editors: vim swap, backup and netrw files, tags (and the .tags.* file
# git ctags writes while it rebuilds them), IDE project folders.
# `tags` also hides a directory of that name (a site's tags/ pages).
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.*.sw?
.netrwhist
tags
.tags.*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.sublime-workspace

# Operating systems: macOS Finder and resource files, Windows thumbnails.
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Environments and tool caches: local .env overrides, direnv, virtualenvs,
# python caches.
.env.local
.direnv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Coding agents' per-user settings.
**/.claude/settings.local.json

# Coding agents' instruction and handoff files, at a repository's root only,
# so a project whose product is agent config (skills/agent-config/) can still
# commit its own.  They never belong in a repository.
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/GEMINI.md
/HANDOFF.md
/.claude/
/.agent/
/.agents/
/.gemini/

# Merge and patch leftovers: *.orig from mergetool, *.rej from a failed patch.
#*.orig
#*.rej

# Jupyter's checkpoint copies.
#.ipynb_checkpoints/

# direnv's .envrc itself, when it holds secrets or machine paths.
#.envrc

# Python packaging output: egg-info, dist.
#*.egg-info/
#dist/

# Coverage data and tox environments.
#.coverage
#.tox/

# C and C++ tool state: clangd's cache, compile_commands.json.
#.cache/clangd/
#compile_commands.json

# node dependencies (usually already in the project's .gitignore).
#node_modules/

# Log files anywhere.
#*.log
